<section>
    <section id="test11">
        <h2>Is color alone not used to convey information? </h2>
        <p>Pay attention to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Links in paragraphs </li>
            <li>Form validation</li>
            <li>Custom form fields</li>
            <li>Diagrams</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Not OK : use of color only to identify links</h2>
        <p><img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/color/belfius_link.jpg" alt="blue link (not underlined) in paragraph of black text"></p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Not OK : use of color only to identify error in form</h2>
        <p><img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/color/belfius_form_error_nok.jpg" alt="Form field with red outline but no error message"></p>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h2>OK : use of color and text to identify error in form</h2>
        <p><img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/color/belfius_form_error_ok.jpg" alt="Form field with red outline and error message"></p>
    </section>

            <section>
        <h2>OK : use of color and text to identify data in a diagram</h2>
        <p><img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/color/belfius_diagram_ok.jpg" alt="donut diagram with percentages repeated in the legend"></p>
    </section>
</section>
